WEBVTT

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.080
<i>Anshin Loan</i>

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.830
As for the rest, go do as we arranged then.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.090
I understand.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:38.700
Tanishi!

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.200
Yes?

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.970
Couldn't you do anything about this?

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:45.530
Well, we couldn't just swap
what was inside.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.540
I hope they get out of the way soon.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.490
Aren't you smart enough to think
about painting over this?

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.990
I'm sorry.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:01.510
There's no time. Put a sticker
on it to cover it.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.390
If this is seen, it's not a good thing.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:04.450
Yes, Sir.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.070
<i>Norikonda sabaibaru cousutaa</i>

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.040
The survival roller coaster we got on

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.810
There's no need to give up,
run by the highway

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>Akirame muyoude run by the highway</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.380
<i>Kimiwa inochi karagara</i>

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:19.580
You just barely escaped with your life

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.910
<i>Atashitachimo nodoga karakara</i>

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:22.180
We're thirsty

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:24.110
<i>Kyokugento mugendai</i>

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.320
Extremities and infinity

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:26.450
<i>Tomo ni sorette mugendai</i>

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.680
Together, they form a fantasy

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.350
<i>Kamaeta me hibana chiri</i>

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.550
The eyes, squaring away, are
throwing out sparks

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.380
<i>Oni-san kochira to shita o dasu</i>

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:31.610
"You're it! This way, " you say,
as you stick your tongue out

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.610
<i>Wink</i>

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:33.680
Wink

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.290
<i>Kyouretsuna itamini kansha</i>

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:37.500
Grateful for the excruciating pain

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.630
<i>Power to iu na no rei de henkan</i>

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.930
I'm restored by a gratitude
known as power

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:45.540
<i>Mou sorosoro okaeri asobareta houga
iinodewa naide shouka</i>

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:45.740
Perhaps it would be better too return soon?

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:54.440
<i>Matsugeno sukima umeruyouni aimeiku</i>

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:54.680
As though filling in the gaps between
the eyelashes, eye make

00:01:54.440 --> 00:02:01.750
<i>Kokorono sukima umeruyouni I take</i>

00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:01.950
As though filling in the gaps of
my heart, I take

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:06.220
<i>Gekiretsu panchide gyakuni takamaru</i>

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:06.420
On the contrary, the intensity is heightened
by a powerful punch

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:10.690
<i>Yabai shiuchi hodo yokei moechauwa</i>

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:10.760
The worse I'm treated, the more I get fired up

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:15.060
<i>Mouretsu panchide atashi takaburu</i>

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:15.200
I get worked up over an intense punch

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:23.490
<i>Sonna koto shite kurete arigatou</i>

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:24.040
Thank you for doing such a thing

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.010
<i>Sukima sukima sukimani mimai</i>

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.210
A gap, a gap, pay a sympathy visit

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.010
<i>Janai janai itainjanai?</i>

00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:28.180
Doesn't it, doesn't it, doesn't it hurt?

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.680
<i>Mimai tsurai? ltai? Yabai?</i>

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.950
Is the visit painful? Does it hurt?
Is it dangerous?

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.310
<i>lkitai itai shitai, lkitai itai shitai</i>

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:34.620
I want to go, I want to stay, I want to do it

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:45.530
Today seems to be cold too.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.860
Normally, I don't want to go anywhere
on a day like this.

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.670
It's quite simple.

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:57.510
At a specific time, at a specific place,
I would like to have this delivered.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.300
So we're just couriers now?

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:03.140
Since we're being asked to do it, it's
got to be some volatile goods.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.480
What's inside?

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:10.750
I'm telling you, we're being asked to
do this, so of course, he can't say.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.980
That's exactly right.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.650
Will you accept it?

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.630
Well, you see here...

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.260
We're eager to accept it, accept it
on the double, but...

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.500
Doing the job immediately is a bit...

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.970
Well, that is to say...

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:28.970
This office's karaoke contest is
about to start!

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:30.400
Right?!

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.040
What? Wow!

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.340
Payment will be in cash.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.950
Half of it will be paid upfront.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:42.980
Just for being couriers!

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.210
With this price!

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.150
Easy money!

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:51.450
<i>Shell of Fear</i>

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:57.830
Ramen is chewy.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:00.560
I'm glad the extra money was spent to buy
the raw noodles from Natsukiya.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:08.010
How about after this job's done and we get
the money, I buy an entire case of noodles?

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:11.430
What?

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.350
Was your name Asami?

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:18.340
Well, we told you the last time.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.490
It's dangerous here, so children like
yourself shouldn't come by.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.550
What did you say?

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.050
Where's Ms. Mikura?

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.390
Mikura?

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.430
You just missed her.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.560
She was here just earlier.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:39.010
Harada, you know, that
pointy-haired armadillo,

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:40.870
people stare at him all the time.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.770
They're merrily out on a drive.

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.010
That's why you should go home now. Okay?

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:48.840
Okay?

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:58.420
I'm at a bit of a loss. I'm not good
at dealing with children at all.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:01.150
Hair, hair, losing my hair again.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.330
The hair growth formula I bought

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:06.320
with money I borrowed on a loan isn't
working at all! Oh, God!

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:14.040
I thought it was pretty cold and no
wonder. The heater's broken.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.440
For real? On a cold day like this!

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.640
This is such an old piece of junk.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.910
You brought the microphone?

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:25.380
Since I have free time, I figured I'd
get some practice in.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:30.080
With this one mic, it seems like an outdoor
live performance is possible as well.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.100
Now, Asami.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:41.030
Will you please go home when
you're done eating that?

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:45.040
You plan to stay here until
Mikura comes home?

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:47.530
Well, we do have a chair for
you to sit in until then.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:50.810
I'm at a loss. I ought to go pray
over at the Temple of Ise.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:53.580
Well, waiting is all right,

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.050
but she won't be back for another
three or four hours.

00:05:57.220 --> 00:06:01.090
I'm not good at filling time, nor picking up
women, but leave me alone on that issue.

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:04.860
I wonder if there are any
cartoons on? Mezzo.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:15.840
<i>Burglary at the Bio Research Facility!</i>

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:06.960
Now for the next news item.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:11.670
Early this morning, at the bio research facility
in the Kanagawa Prefecture,

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.900
burglars broke in and stole
bacterium samples

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.840
Burglary at the Bio Research Facility!
which were currently being researched.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.670
Culprits still at large!
It appears the group of culprits are
currently on the run.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.310
Some people have strange tastes.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.780
What's the point of stealing germs
anyway, you guys?

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:29.420
This is the same type of case as the one
with the bacterium samples in it.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:35.390
Ow, ow, ow! This is no time for germs!
Where's a rag for this?

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:40.060
Say, Asami?

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:44.430
It's that trunk.

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.730
What? Trunk?

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:51.840
Right now, the refrigeration
device is working,

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.300
but the battery will only last ten hours.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:59.550
If the refrigeration device cuts out and
the new type of bacterium,

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:02.720
the BROP, leaks out,

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:05.250
a horrible number of casualties will occur.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:05.250
No way...

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.280
Say, what's going on? What's the matter?

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.180
Is that true, for real, real?!

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:18.100
Did that case have a sticker on it?

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:20.530
They said, if it was seen,
it wasn't a good thing.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:23.440
This is bad, bad.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.570
Oh, cell phone?

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.770
Oh, that's right. I was charging it.

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:37.440
A kid? So he's not alone.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.160
What's the matter?

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:44.490
Something flashed just now.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:45.850
Flashed?

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:52.500
Well, there doesn't seem to be anything.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.840
Ah, where's that baldy gone off to?

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:08.940
He's the one who said to call in periodically.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.490
It's so cold in this piece of junk.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.960
We're about to hit the mountains
so it'll get colder.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:20.350
In that case... Voila!

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.470
The universe, frightened of imbalance

00:08:33.470 --> 00:08:35.910
We suspect this is not something ordinary

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.850
Our wits collide

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:39.970
They boldly circle around and rise skyward

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.370
Extremities and infinity

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:44.610
Together, they form a fantasy

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.750
The eyes, squaring away, are
throwing out sparks

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.780
"You're it! This way," you say,
as you stick your tongue out

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:51.920
Wink

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.120
Wink

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.290
Wink

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.030
The survival roller coaster we got on

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:02.330
There's no need to give up,
run by the highway

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:04.370
You just barely escaped with your life

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:07.010
We're thirsty

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:09.040
Grateful for the excruciating pain

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:11.510
I'm restored by a gratitude
known as power

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:16.920
Perhaps it would be better to return soon?

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:26.060
As though filling in the gaps between
the eyelashes, eye make

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:33.270
As though filling in the gaps
of my heart, I take

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:37.870
On the contrary, the intensity is
heightened by a powerful punch

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:42.310
The worse I'm treated, the more
I get fired up

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:46.750
I get worked up over an intense punch

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:52.080
Thank you for doing such a thing

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:52.080
You're singing the same song over and over.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:54.680
I'm finally in the groove!

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:57.690
On a highway like this, no one's
listening anyway.

00:09:57.690 --> 00:09:58.990
Then turn down the volume!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:01.150
It's been turned down to the minimum.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:04.430
The universe, frightened of imbalance

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:07.440
We suspect this is not something ordinary

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.440
Say, Mikura. Give it a rest already.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:08.470
What?!

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:12.740
Don't you think it's about time we
contacted the office again?

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:15.330
Jeez, let me at least sing the
bridge part of the song.

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:23.550
All right, go ahead and pass.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:28.350
What the...

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:30.490
Harada! It's headed this way!

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:31.790
Damn it!

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.630
Out of nowhere, the guy wants
to incite something.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:38.330
We're in a piece of junk so we're
probably being looked down upon.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:41.390
I think I'll lower this song's
key by half a note.

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:46.940
He's coming again? What to do?

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:49.780
We're working. We're working.

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:51.840
We won't have anything to do with him.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.330
What the hell is this?

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:07.800
If someone hits us...

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.390
We hit him back!

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.230
Harada, bullets!

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:19.730
Here you go.

00:11:20.510 --> 00:11:21.540
Step on it!

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:22.980
Gotcha!

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:06.620
I'm telling you. All of a sudden,
we were shot at.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:08.690
Hot!

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:10.190
What? Bacterium?

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:11.280
What's that?

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.260
Mikura, let me talk to him.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.530
Is the refrigeration device all right?

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:21.300
It seems to be working for now?

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:25.400
That germ inside isn't your run-of-the-mill
germ. It's some nasty stuff.

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:29.880
If a human contracts it, it takes two,
three days and it's goodbye.

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:31.750
Whoa! For real?!

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.940
Can we just toss it aside somewhere?

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:35.980
What's this?

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:38.790
When it comes into contact with air,
it spreads like influenza,

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:40.050
so that would be bad.

00:12:40.350 --> 00:12:42.690
You understand what passing the date of
expiration does, don't you, Harada?

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:45.130
Passing the date of expiration?

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:45.760
Hey!

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:48.590
That kind of sort-of-understandable, sort-of-
not-understandable metaphor doesn't help.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:51.570
Come to think of it, I feel like I'm coming
down with something too.

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:52.830
Harada, this!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.090
How vulgar.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:59.210
Anyway, this might become the cause
of humanity's annihilation.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:00.940
So be extra careful.

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.570
Then, what should we do?

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:05.750
Harada! Behind, behind!

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:09.320
Well about that, right now...

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:10.020
Persistent!

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:11.290
Mr. Kurokawa, talk to you later!

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:12.510
Hello? Harada...

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.520
This case is their target.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.790
Hey, Harada, take a little look at this.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.460
Now's not the time for that.

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:35.230
Mikura!

00:13:36.010 --> 00:13:38.570
Not yet! Somehow, get through this tunnel!

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:45.320
Damn! Easier said than done!

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:46.840
This tunnel is long!

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:12.410
This is bad. I have a nasty feeling about this.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.220
Where are you going?

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:17.950
Well, I was about to go buy a fried
minced meat cake, you see.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:20.650
I'm in a bit of a hurry, so...

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:24.090
Take me with you.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:26.420
What? Well, take...

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:37.330
No good. How about you?

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.340
No reception at all. After all, we're in
the middle of the mountains.

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:48.810
What should we do?

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:50.870
Should we return this?

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:52.120
Where?

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:53.420
The original place.

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:54.660
You're joking, right?

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:59.820
But if we hand it over to those guys,
we'll end up being the culprits.

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:02.420
Culprits? Of what?

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:04.630
The latest news!

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:10.270
<i>LATEST NEWS
The bacterium robbers are a man and a
woman driving a classical pink Volkswagen,
says a witness. The information was...</i>

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:12.870
The bacterium robbers are a man and a
woman driving a classical pink Volkswagen...

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:14.700
What the hell?!

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:36.160
You idiot!

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:39.500
I'm sorry, Mister.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:42.570
Hurry and get it back. I'll go with you.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:44.170
Yes, Sir.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:47.270
We'd better return this and
explain the situation.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:52.270
Do you honestly think saying the bad
guys stole this will work as a story?

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.570
Nah...

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:55.510
We can't just sit around!

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:58.910
We don't know how long the
refrigeration device will last.

00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:02.320
We don't have much of a choice, do we?

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:08.990
Say, where's the case?

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:12.070
Why, didn't you bring it with you?

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.260
Me?

00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:14.940
Why should I carry it?

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.540
I don't believe this!

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:18.900
You want me to carry that dangerous thing?

00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:21.900
It's only until we get there,
so what's the big deal?

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:23.780
But it's scary.

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:27.110
That box full of germs, if it opens...

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:29.510
What?

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:30.940
Where's the case?

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:33.220
Hey, over there!

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:34.780
That guy!

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:41.720
I won't let you get away!

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:56.780
Hey! You!

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.650
Hey, what do you think you're doing?!

00:16:59.650 --> 00:17:01.310
Thank you very much.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.180
This place is perfectly fine.

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:06.790
So where's the rest of the money?

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:08.620
Jeez!

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:10.590
What a tough-spirited young lady.

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:14.020
Isn't there something you should worry
about other than money?

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:16.720
It's my job.

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:19.590
Those who betray us won't live long
enough to eat dinner.

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.470
You're an interesting young lady.

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:23.740
What's the meaning of this?

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:26.100
Since you're a villain, act like one
and give an explanation.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:30.110
In a certain country, someone
wants to buy this.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:32.100
You could have taken it yourself.

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:33.910
You're a decoy

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:35.950
to mislead the authorities.

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:39.350
We set you up as the culprits, then nab the
goods on the way and dispose of you.

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:43.450
There was someone who offered that idea.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:44.490
What?

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:47.520
You're the ones who play the bad guys.

00:17:48.860 --> 00:17:51.020
We don't play the bad guys!

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:55.470
We ARE the bad guys!

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:04.750
Mikura, hurry!

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:05.870
You're late, Harada!

00:18:12.490 --> 00:18:13.680
Hey, there he is!

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.950
Just slow him down! If the case
pops open, it's all over.

00:18:18.460 --> 00:18:19.720
I know!

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:32.540
They took him!

00:18:32.810 --> 00:18:34.140
Damn!

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:51.460
They had something like that?!

00:18:51.460 --> 00:18:52.360
Harada, bullets!

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:56.360
There aren't any left.

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:57.590
For real?

00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.960
We don't have a choice but
to withdraw for now.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:01.860
If they escape, it's over!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.310
Where are they?

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:10.680
They're not following us.

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:13.040
How smart of them.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:16.250
This is PA.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.090
I've received the goods, safe and sound.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:20.620
I'll bring it to you right away.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:21.820
Mister!

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:22.720
I'm busy right now!

00:19:22.720 --> 00:19:23.890
It's them!

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:24.920
What?

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:28.490
They don't know when to quit.

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:31.890
Just the punk?

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:33.620
Can we really go on like this?

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:38.800
Come on, let's go!

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:44.900
I can't see what's ahead of me!
I've hit my limit.

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:47.880
It's over.

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:01.520
Little girl!

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:16.870
Don't mess with me, you funky old man!

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:26.250
With this alone, I can do a
live show outdoors.

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:28.790
No doubt, I can!

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.830
If you want to live long enough
to eat dinner,

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.590
be earnest and give yourself up.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:39.560
Mikura!

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:43.300
Yoo hoo!

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.340
I got it back!

00:20:47.780 --> 00:20:49.540
How dare you?!

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:52.040
What? You're still alive.

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:53.980
I'll kill you!

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:58.550
Oh, damn! That hit the refrigeration device.

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:00.280
No way!

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:02.650
Say what?

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:07.800
Hey, trying to get out of here
by yourself? Cheater!

00:21:07.800 --> 00:21:08.630
Shut up!

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:09.690
Look out!

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:15.200
In this case, I'll get away
as far as I can.

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:18.940
The world...

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:20.840
Will be destroyed?

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:32.510
Hey, the school backpack midget!

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:40.160
Looks like we made it just
in the nick of time.

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:44.030
Ms. Mikura!

00:21:42.200 --> 00:21:43.620
What's with this girl?

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:52.440
So they both failed. How boring.

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:56.680
I saw the news and knew right away.

00:21:56.680 --> 00:22:00.080
So, I wanted to tell you that I was going to
borrow a refrigeration truck, just in case.

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:03.450
Then, I couldn't get a hold of you at all.

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:07.180
Then, before I know it, you've been framed
into becoming bacterium robbers.

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.220
So, what's with this dangerous thing?

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:11.860
Something confiscated by the police.

00:22:11.860 --> 00:22:14.730
I pulled a few strings here and
there and it's now mine.

00:22:15.660 --> 00:22:17.870
So is this the scandal of an ex-detective?

00:22:17.870 --> 00:22:20.030
But we're the bad guys, right?

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:26.370
You're so awesome after all, Master Mikura.

00:22:26.370 --> 00:22:28.100
I respect you even more.

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:32.040
Asami, don't call me master.

00:22:32.550 --> 00:22:34.350
I'm not a master comedian or anything.

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:37.750
But I want to be just like you!

00:22:38.720 --> 00:22:41.480
Oh, that girl can actually speak
pretty well after all.

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:44.750
Just as I thought, I'm not good at
dealing with children.

00:22:45.590 --> 00:22:48.820
But thanks to her, we were saved.

00:22:50.630 --> 00:22:54.130
Well, her coming to visit once in
a while might be good.

00:22:54.130 --> 00:22:55.740
Or should I ought to get my head examined?

00:22:55.740 --> 00:22:57.370
Hey, this is karaoke.

00:22:57.370 --> 00:22:59.000
Ms. Mikura, let's sing together.

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:02.100
Somehow, the beat's even
a bit different. Hey!

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:05.900
Hold it right there!

